1. Run when Claude stops (after each response)
2. Copy/sync the conversation JSONL files to a date-organized folder in the DAS-claudecode repo
3. Commit and push

The hook will be a shell script/command. Since this is Windows with bash, I'll use a bash script.

The hook format in Claude Code settings.json:
```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "bash script here"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Now I'm creating a bash script that will handle the sync logic. It needs to capture today's date, create a dated directory structure in the DAS-claudecode repo, copy over the JSONL conversation files, then stage, commit (only if there are actual changes), and push everything to the remote.

